210:   <body>
211:     <header>
212:       <h1>Resilience Weather Station: Judge Sheet</h1>
213:       <p class="lede">
214:         Sheridan Datathon 2026, Tangerine track Resilience Rewired. One page of definitions,
215:         arithmetic, keys, and the rehearsal script, so the demo runs with the site down.
216:       </p>
217:       <span class="tag">Synthetic data: fixture accounts only, no real customers</span>
218:       <p class="screen-only">Press Control + P to print this sheet on one US Letter page.</p>
219:     </header>
220: 
221:     <div class="sheet">
222:       <section>
223:         <h2>The six numbers</h2>
224:         <table>
225:           <thead>
226:             <tr>
227:               <th>Number</th>
228:               <th>Definition from monthly_summary.csv</th>
229:             </tr>
230:           </thead>
231:           <tbody>
232:             <tr>
233:               <td class="mono"><b>I</b> money in</td>
234:               <td>Median of money_in</td>
235:             </tr>
236:             <tr>
237:               <td class="mono"><b>F</b> fixed costs</td>
238:               <td>Median of household_bills + insurance + loan_payments (shown, not used in runway)</td>
239:             </tr>
240:             <tr>
241:               <td class="mono"><b>S</b> spending</td>
242:               <td>Median of money_out</td>
243:             </tr>
244:             <tr>
245:               <td class="mono"><b>B</b> buffer</td>
246:               <td>Mean of avg_daily_balance over the last 6 rows, sorted by month</td>
247:             </tr>
248:             <tr>
249:               <td class="mono"><b>H</b> household bills</td>
250:               <td>Median of household_bills</td>
251:             </tr>
252:             <tr>
253:               <td class="mono"><b>P</b> loan payment</td>
254:               <td>monthly_payment in loans.csv when the loan still runs at the end of 2025, else 0</td>
255:             </tr>
256:           </tbody>
257:         </table>
258:       </section>
259: 
260:       <section>
261:         <h2>Runway formula and rounding</h2>
262:         <p class="mono">buffer_left = B minus one off costs (one off costs subtract from B)</p>
263:         <p class="mono">gap = spending after shock minus income after shock</p>
264:         <ul>
265:           <li>buffer_left at or below 0: runway is 0, band Critical</li>
266:           <li>gap at or below 0: runway reads no shortfall, 120 plus, band Clear</li>
267:           <li>otherwise: runway = min(buffer_left divided by gap, 120 months)</li>
268:         </ul>
269:         <p class="note">
270:           Runway prints rounded to 1 decimal. Internally the engine keeps integer cents and
271:           integer tenths of a month, so two surfaces can never disagree by a cent.
272:         </p>
273:       </section>
274: 
275:       <section>
276:         <h2>Worked example: account 68257</h2>
277:         <p class="mono">I 650326c ($6,503.26), S 716084c ($7,160.84), B 643785c ($6,437.85)</p>
278:         <p class="mono">H 430672c ($4,306.72), P 284493c ($2,844.93)</p>
279:         <p class="mono">gap = S minus I = 716084 minus 650326 = 65758c ($657.58)</p>
280:         <p class="mono">Baseline: deci 98, so 9.8 months, band Fair skies</p>
281:         <p class="mono">Layoff: income after = 0.55 x I = 357679c ($3,576.79)</p>
282:         <p class="mono">gap after = 716084 minus 357679 = 358405c ($3,584.05)</p>
283:         <p class="mono">Runway = 643785 divided by 358405 = 1.8 months (deci 18)</p>
284:         <p class="band"><b>Fair skies becomes Storm warning.</b> The 6 month EI horizon is display only.</p>
285:         <p class="note">Trace: scripts/engine/golden_fixtures.json, account 68257.</p>
286:       </section>
287: 
288:       <section>
289:         <h2>The five verdict bands</h2>
290:         <table>
291:           <thead>
292:             <tr>
293:               <th>Band</th>
294:               <th>Threshold on the shocked runway</th>
295:             </tr>
296:           </thead>
297:           <tbody>
298:             <tr>
299:               <td><b>Critical</b></td>
300:               <td>Buffer gone, or under 1.0 month</td>
301:             </tr>
302:             <tr>
303:               <td><b>Storm warning</b></td>
304:               <td>1.0 to 2.9 months</td>
305:             </tr>
306:             <tr>
307:               <td><b>Watch</b></td>
308:               <td>3.0 to 5.9 months</td>
309:             </tr>
310:             <tr>
